WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.690
Same memory experiment.

2
00:00:01.740 --> 00:00:03.040
Same word list.

3
00:00:03.090 --> 00:00:04.360
Run twice.

4
00:00:04.410 --> 00:00:06.810
Run one: a quiet lab.

5
00:00:06.860 --> 00:00:12.060
Separate cubicles, a timer, identical
printed instructions for everyone.

6
00:00:12.110 --> 00:00:14.890
Run two: an ordinary classroom.

7
00:00:14.940 --> 00:00:15.920
A bell rings.

8
00:00:15.970 --> 00:00:17.120
A door bangs.

9
00:00:17.170 --> 00:00:19.630
Someone at the back won't stop chatting.

10
00:00:19.680 --> 00:00:21.500
Each run gives a result.

11
00:00:21.550 --> 00:00:23.780
So which result should you trust?

12
00:00:23.830 --> 00:00:28.230
In this mission, you'll see why a
laboratory experiment is so controlled,

13
00:00:28.280 --> 00:00:30.850
and why it can feel so artificial.

14
00:00:30.900 --> 00:00:35.000
You'll meet the field experiment, where the
researcher still changes the independent

15
00:00:35.050 --> 00:00:38.270
variable, but in a real, everyday setting.

16
00:00:38.320 --> 00:00:42.380
And you'll weigh up a trade-off:
control against realism.

17
00:00:42.430 --> 00:00:46.680
Your mission: decide which result
deserves your trust, and why.
